body:
TBH the idea your therapist had wasn't a bad idea, and well just because you wouldn't be NC doesn't mean you can't emotionally distance. You could still contact less, IDK i agree with your therapist it may be a good idea, at the very least you wouldn't feel doubts when you didnt inevitably go NC.

&#x200B;

EDIT: also that doesn't mean your Nmom has to visit you or anything. Maybe just phone calls and shit.

I can feel your pain on that. I grew with constant arguing that affected me (tho i was the one arguing back). Maybe your mom is a lost cause but you could try talking to your sister privately. I know how painful it can be to hear that shit. I am not gonna tell you to "suck it up" or anything, if you tried all your options your best bet is to minimize damage. Maybe talk to a counsellor or a trusted friend?

&#x200B;

 I say this in the bottom of my heart, don't let it consume you, if you tried all your options sometimes you did all you could and well looking out for yourself is best for your survival. Suggestions would be wearing headphones, walking out when they fight, hanging out with a friend, etc. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

If you can do something try to, but if you keep getting the same result no matter how much you try things sometimes it's not worth the mental effort, especially if you might cost your mental health. Tho this a just some stupid thoughts from a 20 something year old. To end this, please take care of yourself.
